Translation patch: `binlog::misc` packed-time readers on `ParseBuf`

Change: `my_time_packed_from_binary`, `my_datetime_packed_from_binary` and `my_timestamp_from_binary` take `input: &mut ParseBuf<'_>` instead of a generic `T: io::Read` (their only callers, in `binlog/value.rs`, pass `&mut ParseBuf`). Each byteorder read (`read_u8`, `read_i8`, `read_u16/i16/u24/i24/u32/u48::<BigEndian>`, `read_uint::<BigEndian>(5)`) becomes a private helper using `ParseBuf::checked_eat_*_be` (`read_i24` sign-extends the 24-bit value, as byteorder does); when the buffer is too short the helper empties it and returns `binlog::trusted::read_exact_eof()`, the error of `read_exact` on an empty slice (opaque).
Why: byteorder's `ReadBytesExt` goes through `io::Read` on a generic reader, which Aeneas does not model.
Behaviour: Identical for `ParseBuf` inputs: byteorder reads with `read_exact`, which on `ParseBuf` (whose `read` copies what is left) succeeds with the same big-endian value and advance, or consumes the rest of the buffer and fails with std's `READ_EXACT_EOF` error, which is what `read_exact_eof` returns. Public-API narrowing in the patched copy: the three functions no longer accept other readers.

